DC Motor Control with Current Limiting and Thermal Protection
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Task: 
\f1\b0 Design a Simulink model incorporating motor thermal model (winding temperature rise). Implement cascaded control with inner current loop having adjustable limits. Create protection logic that reduces speed or shuts down motor when current or temperature exceeds safe limits. Test under locked-rotor and overload conditions. Add cooling-down period logic before restart. \

\f0\b Importance:
\f1\b0  Motor burnout due to overcurrent and overheating is a common failure mode. Protection mechanisms are mandatory in all commercial motor drives for safety and longevity.\

\f0\b Market relevance: 
\f1\b0 Essential for safe operation in industrial drives, power tools, and consumer electronics.}